    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "These anchors provide higher frequency, lower latency and slightly lower accuracy than `anchorUpdates`.",
      "ko": "When you reset scene reconstruction, ARKit removes any existing mesh anchors ([`ARMeshAnchor`](armeshanchor.md)) from the session.",
      "sourceHash": "a9b64ca38595c39e286483b477a37e9facdef106180f4c5bb4b1140c0a2a9886",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "Use them directly or in combination with `predictAnchor(for:at:)`.",
      "ko": "See [`checkAvailability(completionHandler:)`](argeotrackingconfiguration/checkavailability(completionhandler:).md) for more information.",
      "sourceHash": "d7c7ab97753bcba42f261bf0254a75f9589475bdf577164b01cf01e72a5db06b",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0001",
      "source": "The array may be empty if the provider is not running or no accessory is tracked at the moment.",
      "ko": "If [`checkAvailability(completionHandler:)`](argeotrackingconfiguration/checkavailability(completionhandler:).md) returns [`true`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/true) and an app begins a geo-tracking session, ARKit provides this state reason when the user has moved to an unsupported area.",
      "sourceHash": "5646b3bd95522c74b46f17cd5a497d102f8e321ff0cd12e51ea390798c874959",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
